  "construction": "Distance-amplified code: one tensor-product amplification step (central three-term truncation of the chain-complex tensor product, arXiv:2609.37231) with the [[6,4,2]] CSS amplifier -- H_X = H_Z = the all-ones row on 6 qubits, reduced form, so r_1 = r_2 = 1 -- applied to the board's [[56,28,2]] entry. The step is the operation the one-shot paper arXiv:2610.02137 uses to build its level map (App. A.2, Def 111: the local cones tensored with the repetition code), with the amplifier swapped: that paper takes k_A = d_A = 1, which preserves the distance exactly but leaves k unchanged (its Lemma 118, H_Q(Gamma) = H_Q(C)) and so cannot move a (n, k, d, w) frontier. Here d_A = 2, so n' = 6n + m_X + m_Z = 364, k' = 4k = 112, w' = 8. The X and Z witnesses are the base entry's stored witnesses tensored with the weight-2 [[6,4,2]] logical (weights 4 / 4), so the distance is derived, not searched: the logical-overlap criterion gives d' >= 2d and this witness gives d' <= 2d. Witness-backed upper bound, not an exact distance. Base provenance: 2BGA (arXiv:2306.16400) on SmallGroup(28,2), from github.com/QEC-pages/2BGA-codes @ 403d194c3f98f0cadc236aecbc4a8b6139ccf23c, abelian.zip, diswtabelian_wt6wtL2_order28_k28.txt, line 1. nonidentity supports a=[4], b=[4, 5, 10]. (family generalized-bicycle, 56-28-2). Distance confirmed at 100000 fresh-seed trials per side (seed 5000, gf2_fast, 10 threads): lightest logical found was 4 on both sides, i.e. the derived distance survives independent search. Packaging: Space Bunny Alpha 1.0.",
